From 05d746658e2e6ba932553fe5c43d6d058063987d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:57:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08056/11362] The anti-selectivity headline reverses sign under
 the gate the live pipeline actually runs

Nine review findings against the Phase-1 best-of-N and Phase-2 depth-horizon artifacts, all
verified against the raw grids before being applied, and all seventeen resulting assertions
proved to bite by mutation.

TWO OF THEM CHANGE WHAT THE ARTIFACTS CLAIM.

FIRST, "dynamics anti-selects for plannability" was stated as a property of the candidates and
is a property of the MEASURE. Same 31 scored stall candidates, same plannable set {ft09 k1,
tn36 k1}: under this harness's out-of-sample criterion (i), 0 of 9 selected candidates are
plannable against 2 of 22 rejected -- anti-selective. Under `shipped_gate_passes`, the gate
`select_trusted_world_model` ACTUALLY applies, it is 1 of 7 against 1 of 24 -- a 3.4x
enrichment in the opposite direction. The two bars disagree numerically on 20 of those 31
candidates (ft09 k1: 0.8 here, 1.0 there), and under the shipped gate ft09 k1 sits in BOTH the
selected and the plannable set, so "no candidate in both sets (0 of 40)" holds only for the
harsher bar. Both directions rest on the same 2 successes, so the direction is undetermined.
The headline now says so, both 2x2s are reported side by side under
`dynamics_vs_plannability.MEASURE_DEPENDENCE`, and the verdict token no longer encodes a
direction the data does not fix: `..._dynamics_selection_sign_is_measure_dependent`.

SECOND, the criterion-(i) yield was inflated by a split that could not falsify it. lp85's
held-out set is 18 rows of which 0 change, so its 3 (i)-passers earned accuracy 1.0 by
predicting "nothing changes" -- a third of the 9 stall-path passers, and zero discriminative
evidence. `heldout_can_grade_change: false` was in the artifact; a regex over every artifact
string finds it in no prose anyone would read. Worse, `i_dynamics_strict` does not filter them
either: its no-changing-rows fallback asks only for zero hallucinated no-ops, which excludes a
wholly inert engine and nothing else, so the bar NAMED strict overpromised. A third bar,
`i_dynamics_change_gradable`, excludes such games outright: (i) is 0.25 (6 of 31 candidates),
not 0.40. Gradability is read off the SPLIT, not the candidate row -- reading it off the row
let lp85's two syntax-error candidates back in as genuine Falses and made the yield 0.2 at N=8
only, for a reason having nothing to do with change prediction. The bias runs AGAINST the
conclusion drawn: discounting lp85 leaves the gradable passers entirely tn36's dead engines.

The remaining seven. (3) `gate_timeout` -- ft09 k5, an engine that existed and never finished
being measured -- was folded into every denominator as a criterion failure; it is now None
throughout, so n is 39 not 40, while `unrunnable:*` stays a genuine False because no engine
exists. (4) Wilson 95% intervals on every yield: the headline 0.0 -> 0.4 is 2 successes over 5
games and spans 0.12-0.77; the underpowered caveat previously covered only the pooled means,
not the delta that IS the headline. (5) `server_exe_is_cuda_build` was `"build-hip" not in exe`
-- a negative path heuristic under a name asserting a positive build property. Renamed to
`server_exe_is_not_hip_build`, with a real positive `ldd` check added and gated fail-closed for
future runs; this run's CUDA claim was always carried by the independent per-PID VRAM row.
(6) Phase 2's three UNDECIDED -> `degenerate_goal_predicate` conversions land at depth 70, not
61, where all three are still undecided -- the bidirectionality argument is sound and I
confirmed it, but it must be quoted at the depth where it is true rather than borrowed as
corroboration for the depth-61 result. (7) That disproved set is {k3, k5, k7} and all three
carry held-out accuracy 1.0; naming only k5/k7 undercounted the anti-selectivity evidence the
sentence was marshalling. (8) The accuracy-1.0 trio {k0, k2, k6} expands 2226 nodes; 2229 is
k4 at accuracy 0.588, and 2226 is what the sibling session independently reproduced. (9) The
plannable set at depth 61 is {k0, k1, k2, k4, k6}; k1 was already plannable at the shipped
depth 40 and is the LOW-accuracy member, i.e. exactly the case that weakens the adjacent
anti-selectivity claim, so the full set is now quoted wherever a selection rule is argued about.

WHY THE DEPTH-70 ERROR WAS INVISIBLE, since it is the more instructive one. The sweep measured
40/50/61/70/100 and the reported row carried only 40/61/100. A row that omits measured depths
cannot contradict a claim made about them, so the omission did not merely under-report -- it
disabled the check. The existing test asserted `n_candidates_newly_disproved_by_more_depth >= 1`
and never once asked at what depth. Rows now carry `at_every_depth`, and both that test and the
new suite assert the depth.

Two defects fixed in passing, neither in the findings. `build_artifact.py` wrote to a hardcoded
`/home/ianblenke/github.com/ianblenke/carnot/results` -- the absolute write target CLAUDE.md's
Test-Run Record Integrity rule 4 forbids, and independently a G2 defect since a fresh clone
would write into the operator's checkout; it is derived from `__file__` now. And the
change-gradable denominator is 31 rather than the review's 32 because finding 3 lands on the
same denominator; stated in the artifact rather than left as an unexplained mismatch.

Verification. The scored grid was regenerated and diffed field-by-field against its predecessor:
two sections added, none lost, and ZERO non-criteria fields changed on any of 48 candidates --
no measurement moved, only its labelling. adversarial_verify: 0 flagged on both artifacts. All 5
Phase-1 process gates still pass, plus a new one requiring the vacuity be named in prose rather
than merely recorded in a nested field. 57 related tests pass. 17 mutations, each reverting one
finding, were run against a scratch MIRROR of the repo rather than in place -- the conductor may
be reading results/** concurrently, and an in-place mutate-then-restore opens a window where
another process sees a falsified artifact. All 17 caught; no assertion is decorative.

No ARC game was played, nothing was submitted, no level was banked, and no quality threshold,
MAX_ACTIONS, or production default was changed.

